# The web export. A build artefact — roughly 58MB, most of it the Godot engine
# binary — that is regenerated by godot/tools/export-web.sh and deployed to the
# Suds-Jack gh-pages site. Committing it would put the thing this repo was split
# out to avoid straight back into it.
/build/
/piritori-godot/

# Node's own noise, if a tool ever needs it. There is no build step.
#
# TWO PATTERNS, not one, and it cost finding out the hard way. `node_modules/`
# (trailing slash) matches a real directory ONLY — git's own semantics, not a
# typo — so a capture tool's local symlink to the global npm root
# (`ln -sfn "$(npm root -g)" web/tools/node_modules`, since ESM `import` does
# not honour NODE_PATH the way CJS `require` does) sailed straight past this
# rule and showed up staged under `git status`. The second line matches a
# symlink too.
node_modules/
node_modules

# Generated sheets from godot/tools. Derived from the engine and the plates;
# regenerate rather than commit.
/stage-template.svg
/stage-contact.svg
